## 7. AI Intent Recognition

Every incoming message should be evaluated for its primary intent.

Supported classifications should include:

| Intent | Expected behavior |
|---|---|
| General information | Answer using approved information |
| Hotel FAQ | Retrieve relevant property knowledge |
| Amenity request | Create a service request |
| Housekeeping request | Route to housekeeping |
| Maintenance issue | Create engineering work order |
| Guest complaint | Acknowledge and assess escalation |
| Emergency | Provide immediate safety guidance and notify appropriate staff |
| Billing question | Refer to authorized staff |
| Reservation modification | Submit inquiry or direct to authorized staff |
| Local recommendation | Provide relevant verified recommendations |
| Dining inquiry | Provide approved dining information |
| Upsell inquiry | Present authorized offers |
| Request status | Retrieve existing authorized request |
| Human assistance | Initiate human takeover |
| Unclear request | Ask a focused clarifying question |

Support multiple intents within one message.

Example:

"I need two towels, my AC isn't working, and what time is breakfast?"

Ren should:

- Create a housekeeping request for two towels.
- Create an engineering request for the AC.
- Answer the breakfast question using approved property information.
- Clearly communicate the outcome of each action.

Do not create duplicate requests when a guest repeats the same concern.

