## 16. Automatic Departmental Routing

Hotels must be able to configure their own departments and routing rules.

Default departments:

- Front Desk.
- Housekeeping.
- Engineering.
- Food and Beverage.
- Security.
- Management.
- Guest Services.
- Reservations.
- Accounting.
- Spa.
- Other custom departments.

Example routing:

| Request | Department | Priority |
|---|---|---|
| Extra towels | Housekeeping | Normal |
| Additional pillows | Housekeeping | Normal |
| Broken air conditioning | Engineering | High |
| Toilet overflowing | Engineering | Urgent |
| Noise complaint | Security or Front Desk | High |
| Late checkout | Front Desk | Normal |
| Billing dispute | Front Desk or Accounting | Normal |
| Suspected bedbugs | Management | High |
| Immediate safety threat | Emergency protocol | Critical |

Routing rules must be configurable by hotel.

Allow routing based on:

- Request category.
- Property location.
- Department operating hours.
- Day of week.
- Time of day.
- Priority.
- Staff availability.
- Escalation rules.

Example:

If housekeeping is unavailable after 10 PM, route amenity requests to the overnight front desk team instead.

Provide a fallback department or designated staff queue when no specific routing rule applies.

